title: "Infinity operad pairs, higher distributivity and spectral Tambara functors"
collection: publications
category: manuscripts
excerpt: 'We introduce an $$\infty$$-categorical model of operad pairs and their associated bimonoidal categories. We study the related concepts such as cocartesian-cartesian operad pairs, algebra pairs and Day convolutions. Using the Day convolution for operad pairs, we can define distributive functors between a symmetric bimonoidal category and a cartesian monoidal category. As an application, we show that for a finite group $$G$$, the operadic distributive functors from $$\mathrm{Span} (\mathsf{Fin}_G)$$ to any cartesian monoidal category coincides with the distributive functors defined by the distributive diagram. Therefore, we show that the connective $$G$$-equivariant $$\mathbb{E}_{\infty}$$-ring spectra are equivalently the spectral $$G$$-Tambara functors.'
